  "body": "**Edit:** My original idea is incorrect. We should fire a `scrollend` event to the scrolling element, but avoid the forwarding behavior applied to `scroll` if possible.\n\nWhile scrollend should have Document and Window event handler IDL attributes, there should be no event handler content attributes on the body.\n\n- [x] At least two implementers are interested (and none opposed):\n   * Gecko\n   * Chromium\n- [x] [Tests](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt) are written and can be reviewed and commented upon at:\n   * https://wpt.fyi/results/dom/events/scrolling/scrollend-event-handler-content-attributes.html?label=experimental&label=master&aligned\n- [x] [Implementation bugs](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) are filed:\n    - Chromium: https://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=907601\n    - Gecko: https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1785102\n    - WebKit: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=201556\n\nI should have caught this in https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/8433, but I think `onscrollend` should not provide [event handler content attributes](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#event-handler-content-attributes) on `body`, but should live with `onslotchange` and friends. Both Chromium and Gecko will fire the `scrollend` event to the element event handler content attribute, but will not fire to a body event handler content attribute as tested [here](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/master/dom/events/scrolling/scrollend-event-handler-content-attributes.html#L63-L74).\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/8461/webappapis.html\" title=\"Last updated on Apr 11, 2024, 4:24 AM UTC (485bf07)\">/webappapis.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/8461/a9b07fb...485bf07/webappapis.html\" title=\"Last updated on Apr 11, 2024, 4:24 AM UTC (485bf07)\">diff</a> )",
